  "Still alive. Day seven without the Sun.",
  "Previously: the Sun went out. Now Kai, Leo and Mia are in Iceland.",
  "Earth's average temperature is below zero Fahrenheit, and falling.",
  "@am_echo: \"Why is it still night? It's noon!\"",
  "@af_heart: \"No sunlight means no blue sky. The stars never leave.\"",
  "So how are Iceland's homes still warm?",
  "Magma heats the rock and water deep underground.",
  "Plants like [Hellishei\u00f0i](hettlis-haythee) pipe that heat to the capital's homes.",
  "Almost nine in ten Icelandic homes were already heated this way.",
  "@am_michael: \"So we're safe here forever?\"",
  "@af_heart: \"Not forever. Earth's inner heat is thousands of times weaker than sunlight.\"",
  "@am_echo: \"What about everyone else?\"",
  "Some could survive in deep submarines, or underground on nuclear power.",
  "In [1977](nineteen seventy-seven), the sub Alvin found animals thriving at deep-sea vents.",
  "Microbes there make food from chemicals, not sunlight.",
  "Vent water reaches about four hundred degrees Celsius. Hot enough to melt [lead](led).",
  "Up on land, big trees could hang on for decades.",
  "@am_michael: \"So how cold [does](duz) it finally get?\"",
  "After millions of years, about minus four hundred Fahrenheit. As cold as Pluto.",
  "Even the air would freeze and fall to the ground.",
  "But people could keep using volcanic heat for hundreds of years.",
  "@af_heart: \"So as long as Earth stays warm inside, we're...\""
 ],
